---
description: ZenBlog Clean Architecture rules - always apply
alwaysApply: true
---
ZenBlog is Clean Architecture, strict inward dependencies:
Domain (Identity entity types AppUser/AppRole inherit ASP.NET Identity stores;
no other infra) <- Application (CQRS/MediatR, FluentValidation, AutoMapper,
no EF Core, no HTTP, no UserManager — use Contracts/Identity ports) <-
Infrastructure/Persistence (implements Application's Contracts/*) <-
Presentation (Minimal APIs, no business logic).

Every feature = Commands/Queries + Handlers + Validators + Results + Mapping,
under Core/ZenBlog.Application/Features/<Name>/. Never put EF Core or HTTP
types in Application. Never put business logic in an endpoint - endpoints
only bind, call mediator.Send, map BaseResult to an HTTP result.

Auth: ICurrentUserService, IJwtTokenGenerator, IRefreshTokenService,
IUserAccountService, IUserQueryService, and IRoleChecker are ports in
Application, implemented in ZenBlog.Infrastructure. Never trust a
client-supplied UserId — always take it from ICurrentUserService in the
handler. Use IRoleChecker for Admin/owner authorization checks.

All responses use BaseResult<T> { Data, Errors, IsSuccess }.
